Adding back a spatial_meta column name

We will pipe the spatial_meta data frame for each sample to an inline function (because of the curly braces) that finds the names of data frame (names(.)), evaluates which name(s) are equal to NA (is.na()) and uses the TRUEs and FALSEs that this returns to specify which name needs to be renamed with the specified name (&lt;- "cell_area"). Finally the semicolon followed by a period (; .) is used to tag on another command, in this case to return the data frame after the name has been changed.

for (sample_name in names(scz_spatial@spatial_meta)){
    scz_spatial@spatial_meta[[sample_name]] &lt;- scz_spatial@spatial_meta[[sample_name]] %&gt;%
        { names(.)[is.na(names(.))] &lt;- "cell_area"; . }
}
